<article class="env-definition" id="06WJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06WJ">Definition <span data-tag="06WJ">96.12.1</span>.</a> Let $p : \mathcal{X} \to (\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$ be a category fibred in groupoids. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a presheaf of $\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {X}$-modules. We say $\mathcal{F}$ is <em>locally quasi-coherent</em><a class="footnotemark" href="#a0001665422" id="a0001665422-mark"><sup>1</sup></a> if $\mathcal{F}$ is a sheaf for the étale topology and for every object $x$ of $\mathcal{X}$ the restriction $x^*\mathcal{F}|_{U_{\acute{e}tale}}$ is a quasi-coherent sheaf. Here $U = p(x)$. </p>
</article>